# Local-only stand-in for the Cloudflare Access identity provider.
#
# `pnpm dev-keys` writes a real .dev.vars from a freshly generated RS256 pair:
# the public half lands here as DEV_JWKS, the private half in e2e/.dev-key.json
# (gitignored) where `pnpm dev-token` signs test cookies with it.
#
# src/worker/auth/verify.ts only consults DEV_JWKS when the request hostname is
# localhost, and it still checks signature, issuer and audience. There is no
# bypass path - a local token is a real token from a local issuer.
TEAM_DOMAIN="https://localhost-team.cloudflareaccess.com"
POLICY_AUD="local-development-audience"
DEV_JWKS='{"keys":[]}'
